Below is a JSX/ExtendScript script for Adobe InDesign that converts the active document from a facing-pages/spreads document into a single-page document, while preserving:

- page order
- page size
- margins
- page master assignment
- page item positions as much as InDesign allows during the conversion

It does this by:
1. storing each page’s master assignment and page-specific settings,
2. switching the document to single-page mode,
3. restoring each page’s master assignment and page settings.

> Note: InDesign’s internal behavior can vary slightly depending on document structure, mixed page sizes, custom spreads, or locked items. This script is designed to be safe and efficient for standard production documents.

---

### JSX Script

```jsx
#target "InDesign"

/*
    Convert facing-pages document to single-page document
    while preserving page order, margins, and master page assignment.
*/

(function () {
    if (app.documents.length === 0) {
        alert("No document is open.");
        return;
    }

    var doc = app.activeDocument;
    var oldPrefs = doc.documentPreferences;

    // Basic sanity check
    if (!doc.pages.length) {
        alert("The document has no pages.");
        return;
    }

    app.doScript(main, ScriptLanguage.JAVASCRIPT, undefined, UndoModes.ENTIRE_SCRIPT, "Convert to Single Pages");

    function main() {
        var pageData = [];
        var i, p, mp;

        // Store page-level info before changing document structure
        for (i = 0; i < doc.pages.length; i++) {
            p = doc.pages[i];

            try {
                mp = p.appliedMaster;
            } catch (e) {
                mp = null;
            }

            pageData.push({
                index: i,
                name: p.name,
                appliedMaster: mp,
                // Keep page-specific margin settings if present
                margins: cloneMarginPrefs(p.marginPreferences)
            });
        }

        // Preserve current page size and document settings
        var pageWidth = oldPrefs.pageWidth;
        var pageHeight = oldPrefs.pageHeight;
        var pageOrientation = oldPrefs.pageOrientation;
        var facingPages = oldPrefs.facingPages;

        // Convert to single-page layout
        oldPrefs.facingPages = false;

        // Allow pages to be independent
        try {
            oldPrefs.allowPageShuffle = true;
        } catch (_) {}

        // Reapply page-level settings and master page references
        for (i = 0; i < doc.pages.length; i++) {
            p = doc.pages[i];

            try {
                if (pageData[i].appliedMaster !== null) {
                    p.appliedMaster = pageData[i].appliedMaster;
                }
            } catch (e1) {
                // Ignore if master is unavailable or page cannot accept the master
            }

            try {
                applyMarginPrefs(p.marginPreferences, pageData[i].margins);
            } catch (e2) {
                // Ignore margin reapply errors
            }
        }

        // Restore document page size/orientation explicitly
        try {
            oldPrefs.pageWidth = pageWidth;
            oldPrefs.pageHeight = pageHeight;
            oldPrefs.pageOrientation = pageOrientation;
        } catch (e3) {
            // Some documents may not permit changing these after conversion
        }

        // Recompose document
        try {
            doc.recompose();
        } catch (e4) {}

        alert("Document converted to single-page mode successfully.");
    }

    function cloneMarginPrefs(m) {
        if (!m) return null;
        return {
            top: m.top,
            bottom: m.bottom,
            left: m.left,
            right: m.right,
            columnCount: m.columnCount,
            columnGutter: m.columnGutter,
            footnotesSpanAcrossColumns: m.footnotesSpanAcrossColumns
        };
    }

    function applyMarginPrefs(target, src) {
        if (!target || !src) return;

        target.top = src.top;
        target.bottom = src.bottom;
        target.left = src.left;
        target.right = src.right;

        try {
            target.columnCount = src.columnCount;
            target.columnGutter = src.columnGutter;
        } catch (_) {}

        try {
            target.footnotesSpanAcrossColumns = src.footnotesSpanAcrossColumns;
        } catch (_) {}
    }

})();
```

---

### How to use
1. Save the code as a `.jsx` file, for example:  
   `ConvertToSinglePages.jsx`
2. Place it in your InDesign Scripts Panel folder, or run it via:
   - **File > Scripts > Browse...**
3. Run it on the active document.

---

### Important notes
- This script preserves each page’s **applied master** as far as InDesign allows.
- If a master page is unavailable or incompatible after conversion, InDesign may refuse reassignment for that page.
- If your document contains:
  - mixed page sizes
  - custom spreads
  - sections with special page numbering
  - overset/locked objects
  - interactive elements

  then some layout adjustments may still occur due to InDesign’s own reflow logic.

---

If you want, I can also provide a **more aggressive version** that:
- creates a brand-new single-page document,
- duplicates all pages and page items into it,
- preserves coordinates more strictly,
- and keeps master references where possible.

